{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-205039-r4512966","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Mexican Rice Pilaf","sourcePageId":205039,"sourceRevision":"4512966","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T00:11:08Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Mexican%20Rice%20Pilaf&oldid=4512966","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:34.316Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Mexican recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using habanero","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using tequila","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Side dish recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"c07240a487f9a65f76d2b103d9e3e1ea9ada587ff65d8c55f82c61cd04a9f012","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThere's a lot of Mexican flavors in this dish, like tequila, Mexican oregano, chile powder, habanero chiles, tomato paste, and rice.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] uncooked white [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] unsalted [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*¾ cup [[Cookbook:Tequila|tequila]]\n*¾ cup [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n*2 ½ cups [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] [[Cookbook:Broth|broth]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*¼ tsp freshly-ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Habanero|habanero]] chiles, stemmed\n*1 tbsp dried Mexican [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Rinse rice with cold water until water runs clear. Pat dry with [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]].\n#Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add rice and cook until rice turns golden brown.\n#Meanwhile, combine tequila, broth, tomato, salt, oregano, and pepper. Pour over rice and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Add bay leaves and habanero chiles.\n#Cook, stirring occasionally, 30 minutes or until rice reaches the desired tenderness. \n#Remove bay leaves and chiles. Serve warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Mexican recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tequila]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using habanero]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mexican Rice Pilaf","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups uncooked white rice","sourceText":"2 cups uncooked white rice","amountText":"2 cups uncooked white rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 Tbsp unsalted butter","sourceText":"2 Tbsp unsalted butter","amountText":"2 Tbsp unsalted butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¾ cup tequila","sourceText":"¾ cup tequila","amountText":"¾ cup tequila","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"¾ cup tomato paste","sourceText":"¾ cup tomato paste"